      "role": "user",
      "content": "Wait, \"giant goblin\"? I'm not sure I follow that analogy at all. I'm looking for a technical explanation of the density stratification. Can you just stick to the fluid dynamics and how the pressure-induced changes in the coefficients affect the stability? I'm seeing some really strange, erratic spikes in the salinity sensor readings that don't align with the temp profile. Could you help me figure out if that's a physical phenomenon or a sensor issue?",
      "source": "evaluator"
